{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 48,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.48.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.48.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Great is Jehovah, and greatly to be praised,\nIn the city of our God, in his holy mountain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.48.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.48.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Beautiful in elevation, the joy of the whole earth,\nIs mount Zion, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "on",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the sides of the north,\nThe city of the great King.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.48.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.48.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God hath made himself known in her palaces for a refuge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.48.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.48.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For, lo, the kings assembled themselves,\nThey passed by together.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.48.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.48.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They saw it, then were they amazed;\nThey were dismayed, they hasted away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.48.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.48.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Trembling took hold of them there,\nPain, as of a woman in travail.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.48.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.48.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With the east wind\nThou breakest the ships of Tarshish.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.48.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.48.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As we have heard, so have we seen\nIn the city of Jehovah of hosts, in the city of our God:\nGod will establish it for ever. [Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.48.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.48.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We have thought on thy lovingkindness, O God,\nIn the midst of thy temple.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.48.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.48.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As is thy name, O God,\nSo is thy praise unto the ends of the earth:\nThy right hand is full of righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.48.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.48.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let mount Zion be glad,\nLet the daughters of Judah rejoice,\nBecause of thy judgments.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.48.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.48.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Walk about Zion, and go round about her;\nNumber the towers thereof;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.48.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.48.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Mark ye well her bulwarks;Consider her palaces:\nThat ye may tell it to the generation following.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.48.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.48.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For this God is our God for ever and ever:\nHe will be our guide ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " unto death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ],
  "headings": [
    {
      "style": "s1",
      "text": "The beauty and glory of Zion.",
      "before_verse": 1
    },
    {
      "style": "d",
      "text": "A Song; a Psalm of the sons of Korah.",
      "before_verse": 1
    }
  ]
}
